diff --git a/metal/OPTIMIZATION.md b/metal/OPTIMIZATION.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..ecf19cf1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/metal/OPTIMIZATION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,172 @@
+# Owned Metal resources and experimental multiscale fusion
+
+Production inversion and prediction degridding remain ducc0. After command-line
+parsing, `-mgpu` registers prediction only by default. Same-binary CPU controls
+register no Metal hook. No real-MS measurement or speedup is claimed here.
+
+## Controls
+
+| Environment variable | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| `MX_METAL_MEMORY_MB` | Aggregate owned-buffer budget in integer MiB. Default **1024 only when unset**; decimal digits only, range **1..65536**. Explicit invalid/empty/zero/negative/overflow values disable buffer allocations (zero budget) and emit an unconditional diagnostic. Read once, at first backend budget use. |
+| `MX_METAL_CONVOLVE=1` | Register immutable-owner batch convolution after parsed `-mgpu`. |
+| `MX_METAL_FUSE=1` | Additionally register resident weighted-peak convolution; also requires `MX_METAL_CONVOLVE=1`. |
+| `MX_METAL_NO_FUSE=1` | Override fusion registration and decline direct fusion requests. |
+| `MX_METAL_NO_PLAN_CACHE=1` | Disable retention/reuse of convolution plans and their underlying buffers. |
+| `MX_METAL_NO_KERNEL_CACHE=1` | Disable immutable GPU kernel residency independently of plan reuse. |
+| `MX_METAL_PREDICT_SERIAL=1` | Wait immediately after prediction submit, then return the latched result at the original ordered wait point. Still exactly two slots; proof line reports `serial_waits`. |
+| `MX_METAL_DEBUG_TIMING=1`, `MX_METAL_PROFILE=1` | Emit proof counters/fallback reasons; PROFILE also retains existing spans and adds pool-hit/fusion spans. |
+
+Existing `MX_METAL_NO_CONVOLVE`, `MX_METAL_SINGLE_CONVOLVE`, `MX_METAL_PEAK`,
+`MX_METAL_NO_PEAK`, and `MX_METAL_NO_PREDICT` controls remain available. Boolean
+controls treat unset, empty, and `0` as false.
+
+The budget charges each owned Metal buffer's requested capacity rounded up to
+16 KiB. It includes prediction planes, convolution input/output, resident
+kernels, peak arenas, and **every VkFFT Metal allocation site**, including LUTs,
+Bluestein/Rader work, staging, temporary buffers and dispatch push constants.
+Reservations happen before allocation. A token associated with the actual
+MTLBuffer releases the charge at final object destruction, including command
+buffer retains. Resource ownership and idle reclamation use a shared recursive
+gate; accounting releases use a separate lock, allowing Metal completion threads
+to release buffers while the host waits. Allocation overflow/refusal returns the
+CPU path without publishing partial output.
+
+This caps the sum of **requested lengths rounded to 16 KiB**. It is not a
+proven bound on `MTLBuffer::allocatedSize` or physical allocations; no
+conservative physical-allocation guarantee is claimed. It does not cap
+whole-process RSS, driver backing/pipeline/compiler overhead, other applications, CPU images/FFT caches, or
+the separately quarantined retired inversion/gridding archive. The buffer budget
+must not be represented as a process memory cap.
+
+## Reuse and interfaces
+
+* The process-wide convolution LRU retains at most **4 exact (width,height,batch)
+  plans**, including their real FFT, image-input and resident-peak scratch
+  buffers. The single-C2R hook uses this pool too; no thread-local FFT cache.
+* The shared immutable-kernel LRU retains at most **64 entries**, keyed by
+  `(owner generation,width,height)`, independent of batch plan. Active shared
+  owners pin entries. When all 64 entries are pinned, new buffers remain
+  uncached and are released with their active owners. Other consumers reclaim
+  idle plan/kernel/legacy-peak allocations before budget refusal. No in-flight allocation is evicted.
+* Radler's `KernelFftCache::Fft::Generation()` supplies a monotonic immutable
+  owner/revision token **only on immutable published snapshots**. Mutable
+  vectors (including copies/moves of published values) have token zero, so
+  inherited mutable UVector operations cannot invalidate a resident identity.
+  Publication copies into detached storage: escaped maker pointers cannot
+  mutate a snapshot. Vector construction, assignment and vector-returning makers
+  remain compatible. Cache hits retain tokens; fresh snapshots get new tokens,
+  including after address reuse. At token exhaustion, zero disables residency.
+  `shared_ptr<const Fft>` owns the snapshot for the whole call.
+* Additive Radler setters: `SetOwnedBatchTransformHook`, `SetFusedTransformHook`;
+  production entries: `mx_convolve_many_owned`, `mx_convolve_peak_many`.
+  Existing `SetBatchTransformHook`, `mx_convolve_many`, and `mx_convolve_c2r`
+  remain source-compatible. Unknown/mutable spectra use token zero/null and
+  upload each call. Nonzero tokens promise immutability; never invent them from
+  a data pointer.
+* `mx_convolve_get_stats`, `mx_convolve_clear_cache`, `mx::metal::budgetStats`
+  provide snapshots/idle reclamation. Output-copy bytes count full image row
+  copies, not driver traffic or metadata reads. Kernel bytes count uploads.
+
+Fusion is explicitly limited to **ARM64 builds using the scalar peak oracle**
+(`__aarch64__`, without `__AVX__` or `__SSE__`). Unsupported builds reject
+registration and direct backend reduction/fusion calls, retaining their actual
+CPU oracle. In particular, Intel AVX no-candidate semantics are unchanged.
+
+Fusion consumes resident **padded** inverse FFT output and per-scale masks and
+borders. It returns signed weighted peaks, exact row-major ties, found flags and
+coordinates. Radler performs the original normalization and OptionalNumber
+mapping. Requested CPU images stay **unweighted**. RMS requests force readback
+and use the existing sequential float accumulation. With neither CPU images nor
+RMS, full output-image copies are skipped.
+
+The reduction uses the binary32 weighting implementation shared with the CPU
+arithmetic probe, preserving subnormal, signed zero, NaN/inf and FLT_MIN behavior
+without relying on device denormal handling. Selection is tested against actual
+Radler `peak_finder`, not a copied oracle. Current fusion uses **two ordered GPU
+submissions** (convolution then resident reduction), with a CPU merge of tile
+metadata. It avoids image round-trips but does not yet combine encoding into one
+command buffer. Native shader/FFT/end-to-end correctness and performance remain
+parent-run gates; there is no GPU device or standalone Metal compiler in this
+sandbox.
+
+## Native probes (no Measurement Set needed)
+
+Build from the repository root:
+
+```sh
+/opt/homebrew/bin/cmake --build build-mx-metal -j4 --target wsclean \
+  mx-budget-probe mx-budget-lifetime-probe mx-binary32-probe \
+  mx-prediction-schedule-probe mx-kernel-identity-probe \
+  mx-failure-probe mx-metal-buffer-probe mx-fusion-scope-probe \
+  mx-reuse-probe mx-fusion-probe mx-fusion-public-probe \
+  mx-vkfft-real-probe mx-multiscale-batch-probe mx-peak-probe \
+  mx-prediction-cpu-probe mx-prediction-mock-probe mx-prediction-gpu-probe
+```
+
+CPU/device-independent gates:
+
+```sh
+build-mx-metal/metal/mx-budget-probe
+MX_METAL_MEMORY_MB=1 build-mx-metal/metal/mx-budget-probe 1
+MX_METAL_MEMORY_MB=invalid build-mx-metal/metal/mx-budget-probe 0
+build-mx-metal/metal/mx-budget-lifetime-probe
+build-mx-metal/metal/mx-binary32-probe
+build-mx-metal/metal/mx-kernel-identity-probe
+build-mx-metal/metal/mx-prediction-schedule-probe
+build-mx-metal/metal/mx-fusion-scope-probe
+python3 work/wsclean/metal/review_source_regression.py
+build-mx-metal/metal/mx-fusion-public-probe --cpu
+build-mx-metal/metal/mx-prediction-cpu-probe
+build-mx-metal/metal/mx-prediction-mock-probe
+```
+
+Parent must run these sequentially **outside the sandbox**, before timing:
+
+```sh
+MX_METAL_DEBUG_TIMING=1 build-mx-metal/metal/mx-reuse-probe
+MTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1 build-mx-metal/metal/mx-failure-probe
+MTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1 build-mx-metal/metal/mx-metal-buffer-probe
+build-mx-metal/metal/mx-fusion-probe
+build-mx-metal/metal/mx-fusion-public-probe
+build-mx-metal/metal/mx-vkfft-real-probe
+build-mx-metal/metal/mx-multiscale-batch-probe
+build-mx-metal/metal/mx-peak-probe
+MX_METAL_DEBUG_TIMING=1 build-mx-metal/metal/mx-prediction-gpu-probe
+MX_METAL_DEBUG_TIMING=1 MX_METAL_PREDICT_SERIAL=1 build-mx-metal/metal/mx-prediction-gpu-probe
+```
+
+New GPU gates fail explicitly if a device is absent. The existing prediction GPU
+probe returns **77** after its CPU fallback checks when native validation is
+unavailable; that is not a GPU pass. RED logs and actual sandbox build/test logs
+are under `bench/out/gpu-opt-20261022-153051/native-*`. Parent owns real-MS runs,
+paired cache/fusion/serial ablations, reporting, patch export, and commits.
+
+## Review-fix regression receipts
+
+The `fix-*` receipts in `bench/out/gpu-opt-20261022-153051/` distinguish CPU
+runs, compilation failures, source-only cleanup/scope assertions, and native
+GPU unavailability. The existing `host-native-public-fusion.log`,
+`host-native-fusion.log`, and `public-fusion.log` remain RED host receipts.
+The reserved MSL identifier `half` was renamed `halfway` in the shared
+CPU/MSL arithmetic implementation without changing formulas or tolerances.
+The binary32 CPU probe cannot validate MSL compilation: the parent must rerun
+both native fusion probes.
+
+`mx-failure-probe` injects thread-local allocation refusals at each required
+Bluestein buffer site, a genuine offset-enabled VkFFT dispatch allocation,
+and the resident scratch allocation reached after successful convolution
+completion. It checks immediate planning refusal, cleanup/recovery, and
+transactional image/metadata publication. These are real native paths with
+allocation faults, not fake FFT/GPU success returns. The source-only regression
+also checks all four planning encoder guards; native planning-append failure
+coverage itself is limited to allocations reachable by these configurations.
+
+`mx-reuse-probe` includes two asynchronous FFT owners with 128 distinct
+generations, pin/uncached/idle-trim checks, and output verification.
+`mx-metal-buffer-probe` drops host ownership while an actual Metal command
+waits on a shared event, then checks accounting after completion and final
+command release. It prints requested length, rounded charge and `allocatedSize`
+for shared/private buffers at five boundary sizes; those samples are observations,
+not proof of a physical memory bound. Both new device probes return 77 if no
+device exists; this is unavailable validation, never a GPU pass.
diff --git a/metal/binary32_probe.cpp b/metal/binary32_probe.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..12ebeeb1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/metal/binary32_probe.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+// Compare the exact PRODUCTION shader weighting functions with CPU binary32.
+#include "mxbinary32.h"
+#include <bit>
+#include <cmath>
+#include <cstdint>
+#include <cstdio>
+#include <random>
+namespace {
+using uint=std::uint32_t;using ulong=std::uint64_t;
+int clz(ulong x){return std::countl_zero(x);}
+MX_BINARY32_FUNCTIONS
+bool check(uint a,uint b){
+ volatile float aa=std::bit_cast<float>(a),bb=std::bit_cast<float>(b);
+ const float expected=aa*bb;const uint actual=multiply_bits(a,b);
+ const bool pass=std::isnan(expected)?(actual&0x7fffffff)>0x7f800000:std::bit_cast<uint>(expected)==actual;
+ if(!pass)std::printf("FAIL a=%08x b=%08x cpu=%08x production=%08x\n",a,b,std::bit_cast<uint>(expected),actual);
+ return pass;
+}
+}
+int main(){
+ const uint edge[]={0,0x80000000,1,0x80000001,0x7fffff,0x800000,0x800001,0x3f000000,0x3f800000,0x3fffffff,0x7f7fffff,0xff7fffff,0x7f800000,0xff800000,0x7fc00001};
+ for(uint a:edge)for(uint b:edge)if(!check(a,b))return 1;
+ std::mt19937 rng(1971);for(int i=0;i<2000000;++i)if(!check(rng(),rng()))return 1;
+ std::puts("PASS production binary32 weighting: edge matrix + 2000000 random pairs");
+}
diff --git a/metal/budget_lifetime_probe.mm b/metal/budget_lifetime_probe.mm
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..2f5f5ab5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/metal/budget_lifetime_probe.mm
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+// Exercise production reservation tokens without needing a GPU device.
+#include "mxbudget.h"
+#import <Foundation/Foundation.h>
+#include <cstdio>
+#include <thread>
+extern "C" bool mx_metal_track_buffer(void*,std::size_t) noexcept;
+#define CHECK(x) do{if(!(x)){std::fprintf(stderr,"FAIL line %d: %s\n",__LINE__,#x);return 1;}}while(0)
+int main(){
+ using namespace mx::metal;
+ @autoreleasepool {
+  CHECK(reserveBytes(16384));
+  NSObject* owner=[NSObject new];
+  CHECK(mx_metal_track_buffer((__bridge void*)owner,16384));
+  CFTypeRef pending=CFBridgingRetain(owner);
+  owner=nil;CHECK(budgetStats().used==16384);
+  {
+    // Completion may release on another thread while host holds the gate.
+    std::lock_guard lock(resourceMutex());
+    std::thread completion([pending]{CFRelease(pending);});completion.join();
+  }
+  CHECK(budgetStats().used==0);
+ }
+ std::puts("PASS reservation follows final retained object lifetime, cross-thread drain");
+}
diff --git a/metal/budget_probe.cpp b/metal/budget_probe.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..e2434252
--- /dev/null
+++ b/metal/budget_probe.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+// CPU-only production allocator gate: no Metal device or fallback required.
+#include "mxbudget.h"
+#include <atomic>
+#include <cstdio>
+#include <limits>
+#include <cstdlib>
+#include <thread>
+#include <vector>
+#define CHECK(x) do { if (!(x)) { std::fprintf(stderr,"FAIL line %d: %s\n",__LINE__,#x); return 1; } } while(0)
+size_t idle=0;
+int main(int argc,char** argv) {
+  using namespace mx::metal;
+  const auto initial=budgetStats();
+  CHECK(initial.used==0 && initial.limit==((argc>1?std::strtoull(argv[1],nullptr,10):1024ull)<<20));
+  if(initial.limit==0) {
+    CHECK(!reserveBytes(1));
+    CHECK(budgetStats().used==0);
+    std::puts("PASS explicit invalid budget fails closed");
+    return 0;
+  }
+  CHECK(!reserveBytes(std::numeric_limits<size_t>::max()));
+  CHECK(budgetStats().used==0);
+  CHECK(reserveBytes(initial.limit));
+  CHECK(!reserveBytes(1));
+  CHECK(budgetStats().used==initial.limit);
+  releaseBytes(initial.limit);
+  addReclaimer(+[]{if(!idle)return false;releaseBytes(idle);idle=0;recordEviction();return true;});
+  CHECK(reserveBytes(16384));idle=16384;
+  CHECK(reserveBytes(initial.limit));CHECK(idle==0 && budgetStats().evictions>=1);
+  CHECK(!reserveBytes(1));releaseBytes(initial.limit);
+  std::atomic<bool> failed{false};
+  std::vector<std::thread> workers;
+  for(int t=0;t<8;++t) workers.emplace_back([&]{for(int i=0;i<2000;++i){if(!reserveBytes(4096)) failed=true; else releaseBytes(4096);}});
+  for(auto& t:workers)t.join();
+  CHECK(!failed && budgetStats().used==0);
+  CHECK(budgetStats().peak<=initial.limit && budgetStats().refusals>=2);
+  std::puts("PASS aggregate reservations, overflow, refusal, simultaneous consumers");
+}
diff --git a/metal/failure_probe.cpp b/metal/failure_probe.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..5df0fed0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/metal/failure_probe.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,154 @@
+// Native allocation faults at real production sites. No fake GPU returns.
+#include "thirdparty/metal-cpp/Foundation/Foundation.hpp"
+#include "thirdparty/metal-cpp/Metal/Metal.hpp"
+#include "thirdparty/metal-cpp/QuartzCore/QuartzCore.hpp"
+#include <cstring>
+#include <iostream>
+#include "mxmetalbuffer.h"
+#define VKFFT_BACKEND 5
+#include "thirdparty/vkFFT.h"
+#include "mxconvolve.h"
+#include "mxvkfft.h"
+#include <complex>
+#include <cstdio>
+#include <vector>
+#define CHECK(x) do{if(!(x)){std::fprintf(stderr,"FAIL line %d: %s\n",__LINE__,#x);return 1;}}while(0)
+namespace {
+const char* target=nullptr;size_t hits=0,after=0;bool fired=false;
+bool fault(const char* site){
+  if(fired)++after;
+  if(target && std::strcmp(target,site)==0){++hits;fired=true;return true;}
+  return false;
+}
+void arm(const char* site){target=site;hits=after=0;fired=false;mx::metal::bufferFaultForTesting=&fault;}
+void disarm(){mx::metal::bufferFaultForTesting=nullptr;}
+int preparationFault(MTL::Device* device,MTL::CommandQueue* queue,const char* site,bool rader=false,bool multi=false){
+  auto* pool=NS::AutoreleasePool::alloc()->init();
+  const auto baseline=mx::metal::budgetStats().used;
+  uint64_t bytes=257*2*sizeof(float);
+  auto* buffer=mx::metal::newBuffer(device,bytes,MTL::ResourceStorageModeShared);CHECK(buffer);
+  VkFFTApplication app={};VkFFTConfiguration config={};
+  config.device=device;config.queue=queue;config.FFTdim=1;config.size[0]=257;
+  config.buffer=&buffer;config.bufferSize=&bytes;
+  config.fixMaxRaderPrimeFFT=rader?512:13;config.fixMaxRaderPrimeMult=13;
+  arm(site);
+  VkFFTResult result;
+  if(multi){
+    // Reach the multi-upload preparation branch at a bounded padded size;
+    // the local preparation application and all Metal commands are real.
+    app.configuration=config;app.useBluesteinFFT[0]=1;
+    VkFFTPlan plan={};plan.actualFFTSizePerAxis[0][0]=1024;plan.numAxisUploads[0]=2;
+    result=VkFFTGeneratePhaseVectors(&app,&plan,0);
+  }else result=initializeVkFFT(&app,config);
+  disarm();
+  const auto expected=std::strstr(site,"completion")?VKFFT_ERROR_FAILED_TO_SYNCHRONIZE:VKFFT_ERROR_FAILED_TO_CREATE_COMMAND_LIST;
+  std::printf("preparation site=%s result=%d hits=%zu later_operations=%zu\n",site,int(result),hits,after);
+  CHECK(hits==1 && result==expected && after==0);
+  if(!multi)CHECK(!app.localFFTPlan && !app.localFFTPlan_inverse);
+  deleteVkFFT(&app);buffer->release();pool->release();
+  CHECK(mx::metal::budgetStats().used==baseline);
+  {mx::vk::Fft retry;CHECK(retry.initShape(64,48));CHECK(retry.submitForward());CHECK(retry.wait());}
+  CHECK(mx::metal::budgetStats().used==baseline);
+  return 0;
+}
+}
+int main(){
+  auto* device=MTL::CreateSystemDefaultDevice();
+  if(!device){std::fputs("UNAVAILABLE: native Metal device required\n",stderr);return 77;}
+  auto* queue=device->newCommandQueue();CHECK(queue);
